   ctr images mount - Mount an image to a target path

USAGE:
   ctr images mount [command options] [flags] <ref> [<target>]

DESCRIPTION:
   Mount an image rootfs to a specified path.

   When you are done, use the unmount command.


OPTIONS:
   --skip-verify, -k                Skip SSL certificate validation (default: false)
   --plain-http                     Allow connections using plain HTTP (default: false)
   --user value, -u value           User[:password] Registry user and password
   --refresh value                  Refresh token for authorization server
   --hosts-dir value                Custom hosts configuration directory
   --tlscacert value                Path to TLS root CA
   --tlscert value                  Path to TLS client certificate
   --tlskey value                   Path to TLS client key
   --http-dump                      Dump all HTTP request/responses when interacting with container registry (default: false)
   --http-trace                     Enable HTTP tracing for registry interactions (default: false)
   --snapshotter value              Snapshotter name. Empty value stands for the default value. [$CONTAINERD_SNAPSHOTTER]
   --label value [ --label value ]  Labels to attach to the image
   --rw                             Enable write support on the mount (default: false)
   --platform value                 Mount the image for the specified platform (default: "linux/amd64")
   --sync-fs                        Synchronize the underlying filesystem containing files when unpack images, false by default (default: false)
   --expiration value, -x value     Set the expiration time for the mount and snapshots (default: 1h0m0s)
   --help, -h                       Show help
